Implement configurable layered clade annotations in the Dikarya tree viewer
Implement a polished, persistent clade annotation system in Dikarya's /job/<id>/view phylogenetic tree viewer.
The purpose is to let users create publication-style annotations beside a rectangular phylogenetic tree: a vertical line spanning a clade with a text label beside it. The system must support multiple independently configurable layers, so users can label nested taxonomic ranks such as subgenera, sections, subsections, species groups, informal clades, geography, or any other custom grouping.
The feature should be powerful enough for publication figures while remaining straightforward for ordinary tree-viewer use.
Hard requirements
These are the highest-priority constraints. If compromises are needed, preserve them in this order:
Correct biological identity and persistence
No regression to existing tree editing/viewing behavior
Security and server-side validation
Correct rendering after tree edits
Visual polish
Do not sacrifice identity/persistence correctness to make the first rendering implementation easier.
