Acceptance criteria
The feature is complete when all of the following are true:
A user can right-click an internal node and annotate that clade.
A user can annotate an existing selected clade when the selection exactly matches a clade.
Annotation membership is stored by stable canonical leaf identity, never coordinates or mutable display labels.
Duplicate leaf names cannot cause ambiguous annotation membership.
Annotations persist across reloads.
Multiple annotation layers can coexist.
order: 1 is always the innermost visible layer.
Layers can represent nested ranks such as subsection -> section -> subgenus.
Each layer has configurable font, size, style, text color, and line color defaults.
Individual annotations can override layer styles.
Layer style changes dynamically affect inheriting annotations.
Nested/overlapping annotations in the same layer are allowed and render in sub-lanes.
Labels and bars are rendered inside the tree SVG.
Rectangular layout works correctly; circular/radial layout is not part of this feature.
Visible layer widths are measured dynamically so labels are not clipped.
Hidden layers consume no annotation-layout width.
Rotation and resize recompute annotation positions correctly.
Renaming tips does not break membership.
Pruning removes only pruned members.
One-member annotations are preserved and rendered meaningfully.
Rerooting does not delete annotation text/state.
An annotation that no longer represents one current clade is retained but not rendered as a misleading continuous bracket.
Recompute preserves resolvable user-authored annotation metadata and revalidates it.
Read-only users see annotations but cannot mutate them.
Annotation saves are atomic and preserve unrelated tree-state keys.
Two-tab annotation editing uses documented last-write-wins semantics.
Annotation edits do not require a new undo/history system.
Server-side validation prevents invalid or malicious annotation configuration.
Existing viewer behavior is unchanged for trees without annotations.
No database migration or major new dependency is introduced.
